getRouteLength [SimTalk] - Workplace
Returns the length of the route which a Worker would have to cover to get from the Workplace designated
by <Path> to another Workplace or to the WorkerPool.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.getRouteLength(ToWorkplace:path[, FreelyWithinArea:boolean:=false]) 
→ length
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter ToWorkplace of data type path designates the Workplace which is the destination
Workplace.
• The optional parameter FreelyWithinArea of data type boolean sets if the Worker gets to the Workplace
by walking freely within the area or not.
Accept the default value false or do not specify the parameter to compute the route length between
the two Workplaces via Footpaths which are connected with Connectors.
Specify true to compute the route length in the area, i.e., the route of the Worker, who is walking
freely within the area, would take.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is false.
Return Value
The return value has the data type length.
Is -1 if Plant Simulation did not find a route.
var len:length := Workplace1.getRouteLength(Workplace2)
